        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "af3d512de11a328995d6815a994cc718b63377ab",
            "parents": [
                "98a9dd5184caca3f950d8f77915ce13ac9a31206"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/50/89250/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "mikehqt",
                "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                "username": "mikehqt"
            },
            "createdOn": 1778756912,
            "author": {
                "name": "mikehqt",
                "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                "username": "mikehqt"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Whats the purpose of asserting this GPIO? Who will act on these?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "This GPIO informs the RMC that there is a leak at the front bay of the compute tray FE/BE NICs. It is connected to the CPLD in the RMC tray via an LSC cable."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is the CPLD not doing this on its own?  We should not rely on the BMC for real-time requirements.  Asking us to forward a single from one CPLD to another CPLD is violating that and deviating from the design on other liquid cooling platforms."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "The SanMiguel hardware design does not include a CPLD capable of handling this routing, so the BMC must manage it directly. This implementation follows the vendor's reference design. The leak signal from the MCU can only be read by the BMC via the USB interface."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a bad design.  It means that the BMC is part of the critical path for protecting the hardware in the event of a leak.  When the BMC is rebooting, we have potentially minutes worth of water dumping on the floor and minutes worth of machines running with inappropriate amount of cooling.\n\nI've raised this to the EE side, but for at least this revision there isn't any other option.  I'll merge this commit."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Whats the purpose of asserting this GPIO? Who will act on these?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "This GPIO informs the RMC that there is a leak at the rear bay of the compute tray HPMs. It is connected to the CPLD in the RMC tray via an LSC cable.\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Isn't this automatically handled by CPLD?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "On the SanMiguel platform, there is no CPLD design. These GPIOs are connected to an I2C IO expander that links directly to the BMC, so the BMC needs to handle these GPIOs itself."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "@mike_hsieh@quantatw.com are these events unique or are these duplicated by the RMC?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "These GPIO pins will also generate event logs on the RMC side via the LSC cable.\nEvent Log on RMC side:\n\"message\": \"xyz.openbmc_project.State.Leak.Detector.LeakDetectedNormal\"\n\"message\": \"xyz.openbmc_project.State.Leak.Detector.LeakDetectedCritical\""
                }
            ],
            "files": [
                {
